# Declared packaging exclusions for the installable plugin.
#
# STATUS (verified 2026-08-18, Codex Desktop 0.147.0): this file is currently
# INERT for a local-marketplace install. A reinstall with these patterns in
# place still copied every path below into
# $CODEX_HOME/plugins/cache/coordexp-local/codex-wake-me-up/<version>/.
# Do not assume an exclusion here takes effect — verify against the cache.
#
# It is kept because it states packaging intent, matches the convention used by
# the sibling codex-harnessdock plugin, and would take effect automatically if
# the installer gains support. The practical impact of it being ignored is
# small: an installed plugin only reads what its manifest declares
# (skills/ and .mcp.json), so everything below is inert at runtime.

# Editor and language-server state.
.serena/

# Test and build artifacts.
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Behavior contract and change history. Developer documentation and forensic
# evidence, read in the repository rather than from an install.
openspec/
